                "Ignoring central control can lead to a cramped position."
            ]
        },

        ("e4", "c5"): {
            "name": "Sicilian Defence",
            "plans": [
                "Black fights for the centre indirectly using the c-file.",
                "White often aims for d4 to open the centre quickly.",
                "Black typically develops knights to f6 and d6."
            ],
            "mistakes": [
                "White delaying d4 too long can allow Black to equalise easily.",
                "Black failing to develop quickly can lead to a dangerous attack.",
